{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-heat-equation-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-heat-equation-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of solutions of the $q$-heat equation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-heat-equation-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-heat-equation-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","q-heat-equation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QHeatEquation.unique_solution","text":"q-heat-equation-unique.md","leanSource":"q-heat-equation-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:q-heat-equation-unique\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V</code> be a complex vector space that is the algebraic direct sum <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V = \\bigoplus_j V_j</code> of finite-dimensional subspaces, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q \\colon V \\to V</code> be a linear operator with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q(V_j) \\subseteq V_j</code> for every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">j</code>. (For the function algebra of a quantum observable universe the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_j</code> are the Peter–Weyl isotypic components and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_q</code> is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian of <a href=\"#prop:q-heat-equation-exists\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/q-linear-transforms\">4.21.3</a>.) Write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_j \\colon V \\to V_j</code> for the projections. A <em>solution</em> of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-heat equation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\partial_t u = -\\Delta_q u</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[0, T)</code> is a map <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u \\colon [0, T) \\to V</code> such that every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_j u</code> is differentiable and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tfrac{d}{dt}\\, \\pi_j u = -\\Delta_q\\, \\pi_j u</code>.</p>\n<p>Then for every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u_0 \\in V</code> there is exactly one solution with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u(0) = u_0</code>, namely</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\pi_j u(t) \\;=\\; \\exp\\!\\bigl(-t\\, \\Delta_q|_{V_j}\\bigr)\\, \\pi_j u_0\n  \\qquad \\text{for all } j .</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.21.4","page":"b/prop-q-heat-equation-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":99,"fail":3,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":118},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.QHeatEquation.unique_solution","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-heat-equation-unique.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
